                <pb facs="0789" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Forbes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-12T20:00:00+09:00">December 12, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 12—11:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>259. Your telegram No. 262, December 11, 9 p.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d624-f1"/>
                    In view of the resignation of the Cabinet, I shall await appointment of new
                    Foreign Minister before taking any action unless otherwise instructed. I have
                    just been informed that Inukai, President of the Seiyukai, has been summoned to
                    the Imperial Palace at 8 o’clock tonight. Unquestionably he will be asked to
                    form a new cabinet. As yet there are no reliable indications of its
                    composition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
